  "body": "Automated bridge job `RQ-DRAIN2-PH-07` (pool: devin), single commit on base `e78f74b1f`.\n\n**Tests:** no test command\n\n**Tier-1 (CODEOWNERS) paths, async post-merge review:** test/config/realio-lane-membership.mjs test/verse-workbench-contracts-310.test.ts\n\n<details><summary>Agent notes</summary>\n\n# BRIDGE_NOTES — RQ-DRAIN2-PH-07\n\nRework of six conflicting PRs onto current `origin/master` (`e78f74b1f`), in\norder. All six carried real, unlanded work; none was superseded. Changes are\nuncommitted in this worktree for `publish.sh`.\n\n## Per-PR outcomes\n\n- REWORKS_PR: 3548 — reworked. Extracted staged-update status into\n  `src/core/app-update-status.ts` (CLI `app.ts` now thin, re-exports kept),\n  added read-only `GET /api/verse/app/update-status` (`app-update` workbench\n  family), and a Gear Tray update line that polls the staged status only while\n  the self-update badge has an update to describe (5 min, visibility-gated,\n  404 latches \"not in this build\"). The API module lazy-imports the heavy\n  desktop-update graph so workbench mounting stays cheap.\n- REWORKS_PR: 3539 — reworked. `fleet lane-model-drift` classifies configured\n  lane models against the catalog (ids, apiModelIds, engine tags, historical\n  models, `[1m]` context tags, `-high`/`-xhigh` effort suffixes); unknown\n  models exit nonzero. Core + CLI tests added.\n- REWORKS_PR: 3536 — reworked. `fleet launch-wait` measures claim-to-launch\n  latency from `queue/router-queue.md` + `metrics/jobs.jsonl`, separates filler\n  ids via `isFillerId`, reports median/p90, `--hours`/`--json`/`--help`,\n  bounded read-only.\n- REWORKS_PR: 3530 — reworked (selective). `fleet_job_patch` was already on\n  master; ported the missing `fleet_path_cochanges` MCP adapter and, from the\n  same job family, `fleet_job_current_snapshot` groundwork stayed with 3525.\n  Both registered in `fleet-server.ts` with strict arg validation, bounded\n  output and evidence caveats; `FLEET_MCP_TOOL_NAMES` and the stale\n  `phx-mcp-host-runs-31r9` hardcoded inventory (already missing\n  `fleet_email_outbox_batch_await`/`fleet_release_candidate` on master) now\n  assert via the shared contract. COS reconcile/worker portions of the PR\n  were already landed and not duplicated.\n- REWORKS_PR: 3529 — reworked. Phone gateway now classifies exact COS routes:\n  `POST /api/verse/fleet/cos/ask {text}` as a step-up-free write (like the\n  inbox), bare/`?limit=1-50` `GET cos/list` and `?id=cos-<32hex>`\n  `GET cos/status` as reads. `remoteChannelHeaders` stamps\n  `x-ashlr-channel: mobile` on cos/ask + inbox only; the local COS API treats\n  the stamped header as mobile after the mutation gate, so a mobile-sent draft\n  approved on desktop records on-screen delivery. Approval stays\n  desktop-only — no remote approve route. Stale assertions in\n  `verse-fleet-cos-api`/`verse-fleet-cos-list` updated to the new intended\n  policy; OpenAPI + `docs/COS.md` updated.\n- REWORKS_PR: 3525 — reworked. `fleet_job_current_snapshot` MCP tool replays\n  `jobCurrentSnapshot` at a pinned commit: requires a full lowercase 40/64-hex\n  OID, verifies commit + `origin/master` ancestry before scanning, preserves\n  bounded scan/path limits and evidence-status semantics; rejects caller\n  refs/cwd/root. Registered in `fleet-server.ts` + tool inventory; new\n  real-io lane test creates real git history.\n\n## Commands run\n\n- `git fetch origin master refs/pull/{3548,3539,3536,3530,3529,3525}/head:pr/*`\n  (gh CLI config unreadable in sandbox; PR metadata/diffs read via git refs +\n  GitHub read API)\n- `node scripts/verify-changed.mjs` — PASS file selection, fleet registry,\n  eslint changed files, tsgo --noEmit, web typecheck, realio lane lint,\n  verse sync-I/O lint, dedupe\n- `npm run check:docs` — PASS (`errors: []`)\n- `node_modules/.bin/eslint <30 changed files>` — clean, 0 problems\n- `git diff --check` — clean; no `.github/` changes\n- Targeted vitest (all with `HOME=$(mktemp -d)`):\n  - `test/verse-app-update-api.test.ts`, `test/app-update-status.test.ts`,\n    `test/fleet-lane-model-drift{,-cli}.test.ts`, `test/fleet-launch-wait.test.ts`,\n    `test/mcp/fleet-job-current-snapshot-04-sqc1.test.ts`,\n    `test/mcp/fleet-path-cochanges-04-sqd1.test.ts`,\n    `test/mcp/fleet-job-patch-04-sqb1.test.ts`,\n    `test/mcp/fleet-job-current-04-spw1.test.ts` — 9 files, 143 tests, all pass\n  - `test/verse-fleet-cos-api.test.ts`, `test/verse-fleet-cos-list.test.ts`,\n    `test/remote-cos-phone-17.test.ts`, `test/fleet-openapi-coverage.test.ts` —\n    4 files, 39 tests, all pass\n  - `test/remote-gateway{,-policy-phone-routes-31,-http,-auth,\n    -policy-job-detail-nov01,-fleet-routes-oct31}.test.ts` — 6 files, 51 tests,\n    all pass\n  - `test/mcp/fleet-server.test.ts`, `test/mcp-durable-inbox-recut-31.test.ts`,\n    `test/mcp-fleet-lanes-31.test.ts`,\n    `test/fleet-mcp-bus-observation-oct31.test.ts`,\n    `test/phx-mcp-host-runs-31r9.test.ts` — 5 files, 102 tests, all pass\n  - `test/verse-fleet-cos-reconcile-api.test.ts`, `test/doc-facts.test.ts` —\n    2 files, 12 tests, all pass\n  - web: `app-update-line.test.ts`, `GearTrayUpdate.test.tsx` — 2 files,\n    13 tests, all pass\n  - `test/verse-workbench-contracts-310.test.ts` — 48/48 pass with\n    `ASHLR_VITEST_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000`\n\n## Pass/fail counts\n\n- verify-changed: 8 PASS / 0 FAIL (eslint initially SKIPped — local\n  `node_modules/eslint` was a broken partial install; restored via\n  `npm install --no-save eslint@9.39.5`, then `eslint changed files` PASSed)\n- check:docs: PASS\n- Affected backend tests: 355 tests across 24 files, all pass\n- Web tests: 13 tests, all pass\n- Known environment caveat: host load average ~70 during the run;\n  `verse-workbench-contracts-310`'s sequential import-all-modules case exceeds\n  the 5 s unit-lane timeout under that load (47/48 at default timeout, 48/48\n  with the repo's `ASHLR_VITEST_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS` knob). Not a code failure —\n  the new `app-update` family lazy-loads its heavy graph precisely so this\n  stays cheap; CI load is far lower.\n\n## Net LOC\n\n- Tracked modifications: +188 / -90\n- New files (17): +1567\n- Net: +1665 (excluding this file)\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- `test/config/realio-lane-membership.mjs` gained the two new MCP test files —\n  they spawn real `git` and the lane lint requires registration.\n- `test/phx-mcp-host-runs-31r9.test.ts` previously hardcoded a stale tool list\n  (missing two tools already on master); it now asserts against\n  `FLEET_MCP_TOOL_NAMES` like its four sibling inventory tests — same\n  assertion strength, no weakening.\n- COS phone policy is exact-path/exact-query only; `cos/ask` bodies are\n  `{text}`-only and caller-supplied `channel` is rejected; approval remains\n  unreachable from the phone gateway.\n- Nothing committed, pushed, or published; no `.github/` edits; no secrets\n  printed.\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added remote access to the fleet chief-of-staff: submit requests from mobile, review recent tasks, and check task status.\n  - Added fleet reports for model drift and launch wait times.\n  - Added read-only fleet tools for reviewing a job’s state at a specific commit and finding files that change alongside a given path.\n  - Added an app-update status line in the desktop update menu, including staged update details and job-related delays.\n- **Bug Fixes**\n  - Mobile-origin chief-of-staff approvals can now be recorded without requiring a separate delivery channel.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
